<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Spring and white bids down.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Spring and white bids down.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring and soft white wheat bids were lower Wednesday, reflecting the steep drop in futures at the Chicago Board of Trade, Kansas City Board of Trade and Minneapolis Grain Exchange, dealers said.</p>
<p>Farm sales were light in reaction to the lower prices. Some dealers said many farmers were anxious to forward-contract new-crop wheat, but prices need to rise.</p>
<p>&quot;I have a lot of orders to sell new crop for $4.00 (per bushel),&quot; said a Billings, Montana, dealer, who was bidding $3.76 Wednesday.  </p>
